Thought: The series shows strong seasonality and unstable rankings, so a robust mean of all models may be a good baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: test a weighted combination with inverse-error weights to see if a more adaptive weighting beats the simple mean, given the unstable ranking and strong seasonality.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: The series has strong seasonality and unstable rankings; a robust trimmed mean may reduce influence of outlier models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: test a softmax‑negative‑error weighted combination to see if a smoother weighting beats trimmed mean in this unstable, strongly seasonal series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: ranking is unstable and several correlated groups exist; a per‑horizon best‑model weighting may exploit changing strengths.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"best_per_horizon"}

Thought: Test a simple median combination to see if a robust, non‑weighted aggregator outperforms the trimmed mean given the unstable ranking and strong seasonality.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full","rationale":"median as robust alternative to trimmed mean"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and several correlated groups exist; a simple inverse‑error weighting may give a different weighting scheme than the current softmax or best‑per‑horizon.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error","rationale":"test a basic inverse error weighting"}

Thought: The series has unstable rankings and strong seasonality; a dynamic Bayesian aggregation (dba) may adapt better to changing model strengths over horizons.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: The series shows strong seasonality and unstable ranking; a robust weighting that dampens high-error models while still allowing low-error ones may improve over median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error","rationale":"softmax weighting to reduce influence of high-error models"}

Thought: Use ranking stability hint – unstable ranking suggests picking only the best few models to reduce noise.  
Action: select_top_k  
Action Input: {"k":7,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The series shows unstable ranking and strong seasonality; a weighted combination on a reduced, diverse pool (pool4) may balance correlated groups better.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"inverse_error","rationale":"use inverse error weights on the diverse 7‑model pool"}

Thought: test a simple inverse‑error weighted combination on the full pool to see if the robust weighting improves over median/trimmed mean.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: test a robust weighted combination on the full pool using softmax_neg_error to counter unstable rankings.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: The series has strong seasonality and unstable rankings; a simple mean of a focused low‑error pool (pool4) may outperform a full‑pool mean by reducing influence of noisy models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4","rationale":"average only the 7 best models to reduce noise"}

Thought: test a weighted combination with inverse-error weights but regularized towards uniform to mitigate high variance due to few windows (ranking unstable, high correlation).  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","shrinkage":0.5,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the inverse_error handle w6 (no shrinkage) on the full pool to see if raw inverse weighting improves over previous weighted attempts.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w6","rationale":"use raw inverse_error weights on all models"}

Thought: Try a per‑horizon forward selection weighting on the full pool to capture changing strengths across horizons.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: test a softmax‐based weighted combination on the full pool to see if it improves over inverse_error and mean; this is a different weighting scheme.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error","rationale":"softmax weights may reduce influence of very high error models"}

Thought: Testing a per‑cluster weighted combo on the diverse 7‑model pool to see if a softer weighting improves over the hard inverse‑error weights.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"softmax_neg_error","rationale":"use softmax weights on the 7‑model pool"}

Thought: test a per‑horizon best‑model weighting on the diverse 7‑model pool to exploit changing strengths across horizons (ranking unstable, strong seasonality).  
Action: weights_best_per_horizon  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse"}

Thought: test a robust median on the reduced pool (pool4) to see if limiting to diverse models improves robustness given unstable rankings.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4","rationale":"robust median on diverse 7‑model pool"}

